<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_DeviceState" Id="{83155e5b-c608-4d41-b295-c67628bd27d3}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(* Defines one state of a device (actuator): where its axis must sit and which
beam parameters are permitted while it sits there.

Purpose:
    Hold everything the PMPS governor and arbiter need to know about a single
    device state, so that a state number (nStateRef) resolves to a position
    window plus a beam parameter set. One instance per state is stored in the
    device state table (ST_Device.StateTable, an FB_LinearDeviceStateTable) and
    is normally filled in at startup by F_SetStateParams.

Usage:
    stDevice.StateTable.A_Lookup(key := stateNumber) returns one of these. The
    governor (FB_LinearGovernor) then compares rPosition +/- rTolerance with
    stDevice.stAxis.NcToPlc.ActPos, widens its MPS limits to include that
    window while the transition is permitted and re-engages them around it once
    the move is latched, and trips a fast fault when the live beam parameters
    are not safe for stReqBeamParam. This type describes a state definition; it
    is not the live state of a device.

Objectives:
    - Keep the position window and the permitted beam parameters of one state in
      one place, so a state can never be latched with the beam parameter set of
      another state.
    - Name the position unit explicitly, so a state table cannot be written in
      the wrong unit and drive an axis to the wrong setpoint.

History:
    2019-08-28 A. Wallace  : Created while migrating these elements into the
                             PMPS library.
    2026-11-27 L. Numminen : Added this header and documented the meaning and
                             units of every member.
*)
TYPE ST_DeviceState :
STRUCT

    sStateName	:	STRING; //Human-readable state name for display and logging only; F_SetStateParams leaves it empty and states are keyed by nStateRef
    nStateRef	:	UDINT; //Primary key of the device state database: the state number a device looks up in its state table

    //////////////////
    // This stuff may belong in a sub-class or something
    rPosition	:	REAL := 0; //Center of the state, in the actuator axis engineering units used by stDevice.stAxis.NcToPlc.ActPos (mm on the linear axes this governs, not encoder counts)
    rTolerance :	REAL := 0; //Acceptance half width of the state, in the same unit as rPosition: the state is latched once the axis is at standstill inside rPosition +/- rTolerance, and the MPS limits are then re-engaged around exactly that window
    //////////////////
    stReqBeamParam	:	ST_BeamParams; //Beam parameters (transmission, pulse rate, photon energy range, beam class, machine mode, attenuators, stoppers, apertures) that must hold while the device is in this state; the governor trips a fast fault when the live beam parameters are unsafe compared with this set

END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>